Krita Nova 61 - Brush Panel: dock it to the left, right or bottom edge

Drop the floating Brush Panel (dragged by its grip) within 40 px of the
left, right or bottom edge of the window and it docks there:
- left / right: a column as tall as the window, at the very edge;
- bottom: a row as wide as the window - the panel lies down: undo / redo
  side by side, the size and opacity sliders lie down (filled from the
  left, dragged sideways), the grip moves to its left end.
The window's contents (the dockers of that side, the canvas, the toolbars)
move toward the center to make room, so the panel covers nothing. Dragging
it away from its edge floats it again (standing up, the floating height).
A nudge or a resize while docked goes back to the edge. The space is given
back while the panel is hidden (welcome page, hidden by the user).
The side is remembered (kritarc androidBrushPanelSide: 0 floating, 1 left,
2 right, 3 bottom).

